  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 127 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nRidging is expected to ease up through the week, leaving a weakness \nover our region. This setup tends to be less restrictive to the \ndevelopment of popup showers and storms. However, given a lack of \nnoteworthy disturbances, rain chances Friday into the weekend are \nconfined to the Coastal Plains. A weak front is forecast to approach \nfrom the north Friday, but the current model consensus keeps the \nfront well to our north and weakens its accompanying shower activity \nwell outside of the region.\n\nTowards the weekend, low- to mid-level temperatures are forecast to \nincrease as restrengthening ridging aloft over the southwestern \nUS pulls a continental airmass towards South-Central Texas. This \nmay raise temperatures by a few degrees this weekend. We will \ncontinue to monitor for the possibility of maximum temperatures \nand peak index values near or meeting Heat Advisory criteria for \nareas generally along and east of Interstate 35 this upcoming \nweekend. \n\nRidging is forecast to continue restrengthening early next week, \nkeeping rain chances low and mostly confined to the Coastal \nPlains. It's been a hot start to September for the region, \nespecially with regard to overnight temperatures, and the \nsoutherly flow pattern supported next week won't change that much.\nHighs in the 90s to low 100s are forecast to continue through\nearly next week with mild lows in the 70s.",
